17. Ergo, having regard to the provisions contained in Section 173 it is

 hereby directed that the Report of police officer on the completion of

 investigation shall contain the following: -
(i) A report in the form prescribed by the State Government
 stating-
(a) the names of the parties;
(b) the nature of the information;
(c) the names of the persons who appear to be acquainted with
 the circumstances of the case;
(d) whether any offence appears to have been committed and, if
 so, by whom;
(e) whether the accused has been arrested;
(f) whether he has been released on his bond and, if so, whether
 with or without sureties;
(g) whether he has been forwarded in custody under section 170.
